Unfirom Resource Locator (URL)
  https://user:password@tryhackme.com80/view-room?id=1#task3
  Scheme = https (protocol used to access the website: Commonly HTTP or HTTPS)
  User = user:password (Sites that require authentication
  Host/Domian = tryhackmev (tells which website to access)
  Port = 80 (direct browser to the right service)
  Path = view-room (Points to specific file)
  Query String = ?id=1 (used to search terms or form inputs, handle securly to prevent injection attacks)
  Fragment = #task3 (point to speciifc webpage)

HTTP Messages
  packets of data exchanged between a user (the client) and the web server

  HTTPS Requests - Sent by the user to trigger actions on the web application.
  HTTPS Responses - Sent by the server in response to the user’s request.

  Start Line - introduction message, gives important details about how the message should be handled.
  Headers - Made up of key-value pairs that provide extra information about the HTTP message
  Empty Line - Divider that separates the header from the bod
  Body - Data is stored

HTTP Request: Request Line and Methods
    Request Line (start line) - first part of an HTTP request, which tells the server what kind of request it is dealing with. 
    Three main parts: HTTP Method / URL Path / HTTP Version
      Method /path HTTP/version
        example GET /user/login.html HTTP/1.1
